          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6107557e4606bce76116d395cc5db5ed1f09e61a9174cfbdefdc20a2149a499f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b91c9e9976a840b0b54f9fff727b7230",
      "statement": "Handler failures funnel through AppError::IntoResponse, which maps NotFound to 404, BadRequest to 400, and Internal to 500 whose message is logged with tracing::error! and replaced by the constant string \"internal server error\" in the response; every case is serialized as a single-key JSON envelope {\"error\": <string>}.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/src/error.rs#L45-L61",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:00fe8a91f724201f6e78caa3c905948307b9db5fe8ba6cfe2ceecd212d61698c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_69a148f2baab414c96585bd1cfc2c7e0",
      "statement": "AppError's From impls convert any sqlx::Error::RowNotFound into NotFound(\"resource not found\") and every other sqlx::Error into Internal, and any std::io::Error into Internal, so a database or filesystem failure surfaces as a masked 500 rather than leaking detail.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/src/error.rs#L30-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7891c38d99f6a2dcbb8a3b197995b7a8ffad40216e4f41eb8cd773e097977718:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_88c93670b27c4ce3b5f179d798675f95",
      "statement": "Response parsing and deserialization failures are raised by axum 0.8 extractors (Query, Path, Json) before handler code runs, so they are rendered by axum with plain-text bodies and never use the AppError {\"error\": ...} envelope; only errors constructed inside handlers follow the documented error contract.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/Cargo.toml#L8-L8",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c4e1a38524de633c7cfd8dfba0b6b13f241b9ba38e7727fca7d8ec28ae8e6377:"
        },
        {
