    {
      "id": "claim_74039fffe92b4f17bee569ae2e1a5205",
      "statement": "PUT /items/{id} has replace semantics for every nullable column: item::update binds description, location_note, purchased_at, bought_from, price, category_id and container_id straight from the request, so an omitted key writes NULL, while only name and source_type fall back to the stored value — a payload of {\"name\": \"x\"} therefore detaches the item from its category and container and wipes the other optional data.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/src/models/item.rs#L78-L90",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:af756806e2dd0c843555fd9a38eae9610670d5e9b6c6c4604adaaf638fa55bf9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/src/repositories/item.rs#L193-L220",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5cff64752ed1e8ff4b4031956fe8f0f805891e2c2a2719a97746f1c05d4985fd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_989f8a7ff94b4dc48fc0ac297250346f",
      "statement": "POS-style partial updates for trees are not supported: container::update and category::update rebind nullable fields with .or(existing.field) and required fields with .unwrap_or(&existing.field), so an omitted or null value keeps the stored one and a node can be re-parented but never detached to the root via PUT.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/src/repositories/category.rs#L42-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:176b3fce1ebac1c78c829d3fd19e8b566ad2f6a712b5ac897065bb65db65aeb5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/src/repositories/container.rs#L74-L89",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:68612dd8afb5255bd39019cd0fdaf0e204e02c92f33aa2868b9e22dd0d48a467:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b93b481c59344cd89b5d87c48e8dd372",
      "statement": "Item tag assignment is wholesale replacement: item::set_tags deletes all item_tags rows for the item and re-inserts the supplied ids, is skipped entirely when tag_ids is absent, and runs without a transaction, so an empty array is the only way to clear tags and a mid-loop failure leaves a partial set.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/src/repositories/item.rs#L215-L217",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fdff986e920a1dc2ff7ea5f639427abf65d9a4b0d5f3d1cb885e3b9e7daa7bb0:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/src/repositories/item.rs#L245-L258",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:23c1d372ceaa11749fc284951544317a8f5d7d43abbf22e5015e8c0c1d3dd74c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_27023d5cecbb456c8954c7733289b040",
      "statement": "POST /tags is idempotent by name (tag::create returns the pre-existing row instead of a conflict) and PUT /tags/{id} always rewrites the name because UpdateTag declares name as a required String.",
      "evidence": [
